# Order item requests: add, list, delete, plus validation, ownership and cascade checks.
# Run `npm run seed` first (dummy accounts, garment types, orders with and without items).
#
# START HERE, in this order:
#   1. Send loginOwner, loginStaffOne and loginStaffTwo (each gives a token).
#   2. Send listOrders, listDelivered, listGarments, then createOrder.
#      createOrder is made by staff one, so staff one is its handler and can add items to it.
#   Then work top to bottom. The last section deletes the order, so run it last.
#   After reloading VS Code, send the setup requests again.
#
# listGarments is sorted by name: data[0] is the Cap, data[1] is the Hoodie
# (Hoodie sizes: S M L XL XXL; colours: black grey navy. Cap size: One size).
#
# Local: leave @baseUrl as is. Live: swap it for the deployed URL.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

###
# ---------- LOG IN ----------

### loginOwner -> 200
# @name loginOwner
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "owner-password-123" }

### loginStaffOne -> 200
# @name loginStaffOne
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "staff.one@example.com", "password": "staff-password-123" }

### loginStaffTwo -> 200
# @name loginStaffTwo
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "staff.two@example.com", "password": "staff-password-123" }

###
# ---------- SETUP ----------

### listOrders -> 200 (gives a customerId and a seeded order id)
# @name listOrders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

### listDelivered -> 200 (the seeded delivered order has NO handler, so only owners can change it)
# @name listDelivered
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?status=delivered&limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

### listGarments -> 200 (the garment type ids you need when adding items)
# @name listGarments
GET {{baseUrl}}/garment-types
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

### createOrder -> 201 (staff one becomes the handler)
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].customerId}}",
  "dueDate": "2030-01-15",
  "notes": "Order for the item requests"
}

###
# ---------- HAPPY PATHS ----------

### addItem -> 201 (handler adds a Hoodie, size L, black)
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}",
  "size": "L",
  "color": "black",
  "quantity": 12,
  "designNote": "Logo on the chest, back plain"
}

### An owner can add to any order -> 201 (same Hoodie and size, different colour)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}",
  "size": "L",
  "color": "navy",
  "quantity": 4
}

### A different garment (the Cap), designNote left out -> 201 (designNote is null)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[0].id}}",
  "size": "One size",
  "color": "black",
  "quantity": 20
}

### Staff two can READ the items -> 200 (three items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffTwo.response.body.$.token}}

### Items of a seeded order -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffTwo.response.body.$.token}}

###
# ---------- VALIDATION AND EDGE CASES ----------

### Same garment, size and colour again -> 409 DUPLICATE_ITEM
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}",
  "size": "L",
  "color": "black",
  "quantity": 99
}

### Garment type that does not exist -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "000000000000000000000000", "size": "L", "color": "black", "quantity": 1 }

### Size the Hoodie does not offer -> 400 (the message lists the valid sizes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "One size", "color": "black", "quantity": 1 }

### Colour the Hoodie does not offer -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "red", "quantity": 1 }

### Quantity 0 -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "black", "quantity": 0 }

### Quantity 1.5 -> 400 (must be a whole number)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "black", "quantity": 1.5 }

### Quantity sent as text -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "black", "quantity": "5" }

### Quantity 1001 -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "black", "quantity": 1001 }

### Unknown field -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "black", "quantity": 1, "price": 5000 }

### Required fields missing -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "designNote": "no garment, size, colour or quantity" }

###
# ---------- OWNERSHIP ----------

### Staff two cannot ADD to staff one's order -> 403 FORBIDDEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffTwo.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "grey", "quantity": 1 }

### Staff two cannot DELETE an item from it -> 403 FORBIDDEN
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffTwo.response.body.$.token}}

### Staff cannot add to a seeded order that has no handler -> 403 FORBIDDEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listDelivered.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "grey", "quantity": 1 }

### An item id with a DIFFERENT order in the path -> 404 ITEM_NOT_FOUND (owner, so permission passes)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

###
# ---------- DELETE AN ITEM ----------

### Handler deletes the item -> 200
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

### Delete the same item again -> 404 ITEM_NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

###
# ---------- CASCADE: DELETING AN ORDER DELETES ITS ITEMS (run last) ----------

### Handler deletes the whole order -> 200 (its two remaining items go with it)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

### The order's items are no longer reachable -> 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
# (also check in Atlas that no orderitems document still has that orderId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

###
# ---------- OTHER FAILURE CASES ----------

### No token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/items

### Garbage token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer this-is-not-a-real-token

### Malformed order id -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/not-a-real-id/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

### Malformed item id -> 400
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{listOrders.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/items/not-a-real-id
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

### Valid order id that does not exist (list) -> 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/000000000000000000000000/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}

### Valid order id that does not exist (add) -> 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/000000000000000000000000/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaffOne.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "garmentTypeId": "{{listGarments.response.body.$.data[1].id}}", "size": "S", "color": "black", "quantity": 1 }

### Garment types need a login -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/garment-types
